; Re-measure the tool that is in the spindle now (screen button "Measure Tool").
; For when M6 ran with tool measurement switched off, or a tool was re-clamped.
; Always a slow search from [TOOLSENSOR]Z (no fast approach), so a tool that is
; now longer than its last logged touch cannot crash into the setter.
; Stores the new length in the tool table and applies it (G43).

o<measure_tool> sub
#<tool> = #5400
o10 if [#<tool> LE 0]
    (abort, Measure tool: no tool in the spindle - set it with M61 Q<tool> first)
o10 endif
o15 if [#<tool> EQ #<_ini[VERSA_PROBE_OPTIONS]PS_PROBE_TOOL>]
    (abort, Measure tool: the probe is not measured on the tool setter)
o15 endif
M66 P#<_ini[ATC_PINS]SENSOR_TOOL> L0
o20 if [#5399 NE 1]
    (abort, Measure tool: tool sensor sees no tool in the spindle)
o20 endif

o<_psng_modal_save> call
G90 G40 G49

; spindle off and real standstill (< 0.5 Hz) before the setter
M5
M66 P#<_ini[ATC_PINS]SENSOR_SPINDLE_STOPPED> L3 Q#<_ini[ATC]SPINDLE_STOP_TIMEOUT>
o30 if [#5399 LT 0]
    G43
    (abort, Measure tool: spindle did not stop in time)
o30 endif

o<tool_measure> call [#<tool>] [0]
#<result> = #<_value>
G43
o<_psng_modal_restore> call

o40 if [#<result> EQ -1]
    (abort, Measure tool: search velocity is 0 in the probe screen)
o40 elseif [#<result> EQ -2]
    (abort, Measure tool: probe velocity is 0 in the probe screen)
o40 elseif [#<result> EQ -3]
    (abort, Measure tool: tool setter already tripped)
o40 elseif [#<result> EQ -4]
    (abort, Measure tool: no contact with the tool setter)
o40 endif

(DEBUG, Measure tool: T#<tool> length #<_tool_measure_old> -> #<_tool_measure_len>)
o<measure_tool> endsub
M2
